== kodiak/grizzly thread (4804712) ==
[B]Update 2026-10-22: fix release (Now Playing, At a Glance, SystemUI)[/B]

New builds for both phones in this thread:
[LIST]
[*][B]Pixel 11 Pro XL (kodiak):[/B] [ICODE]EvolutionX-17.0-20261022-kodiak-12.3-Unofficial-fastboot.zip[/ICODE]
    SHA-256 [ICODE]337aaa1445f86a87e30d1e9839df7b55495cb16380445022dc4cbef649066bb3[/ICODE]
    [URL=https://sourceforge.net/projects/denson9874-s-user-builds/files/kodiak/17/]SourceForge: kodiak/17[/URL]
[*][B]Pixel 11 Pro (grizzly):[/B] [ICODE]EvolutionX-17.0-20261022-grizzly-12.3-Unofficial-fastboot.zip[/ICODE]
    SHA-256 [ICODE]789924328f45fcac15a35cb0b7b39816ced4e4742f00d0828c4fc6c906809f4b[/ICODE]
    [URL=https://sourceforge.net/projects/denson9874-s-user-builds/files/grizzly/17/]SourceForge: grizzly/17[/URL]
[/LIST]

[B]Already on the 2026-10-18 build?[/B] Settings > System > System updates has this one: it installs to the other slot in the background, then asks you to restart. Rooted with Magisk? Don't restart from there: Magisk > Install > [I]Install to inactive slot (after OTA)[/I] keeps root. Coming from an older build: [ICODE]fastboot update <zip>[/ICODE] (keeps your data).

[B]Fixed[/B]
[LIST]
[*]Now Playing can be turned on again (it was stuck at "Setting up Now Playing").
[*]At a Glance: the individual options (Live Display and the rest) can be switched off again from the widget settings.
[*]kodiak: SystemUI no longer restarts and drops you to the lock screen when you open Quick Settings right after a fingerprint unlock.
[*]Every build is now checked before release for leftover apps and for association rules that differ from stock firmware, the two problems behind these bugs.
[/LIST]
[B]Kernel:[/B] Espada v3.5 (Linux 6.12.96) by Kevtrejo37: reworked Simple LMK (fixes an lmkd crash), CASS picks little/mid cores by measured power, per-app uname spoof, USB OTG in recovery.
[B]Also from upstream:[/B] Evolver redesigned in Material 3 Expressive, Launcher3 layout fix for display size settings, App Lock focus ring, Markup strokes stay inside the image.

Unchanged: Extreme Charging, the charging screensaver, "Use device MAC" for MAC-filtered Wi-Fi, and the stock CD1A.261005.003 firmware (security patch 2026-10-05). Fresh installs: see the first post.

[B]Support policy, please read before reporting[/B]
[LIST]
[*][B]Custom setups get limited to no support.[/B] That means root modules, Xposed/LSPosed, any kernel other than Espada, or apps from APKMirror and similar sites that don't match this build (Google system apps especially). Before you report, reproduce the problem on a clean install without them.
[*][B]No logs, no report.[/B] Bug reports without a logcat are flagged for deletion. Capture one right after the problem happens: [ICODE]adb logcat -b all -d > log.txt[/ICODE] (rooted: [ICODE]su -c "logcat -b all -d > /sdcard/log.txt"[/ICODE]), then post it with your device, build date and steps to reproduce.
[/LIST]

